  "stem": "A homogeneous chain of length L lies on a table. The coefficient of friction between the chain and the table is μ. The maximum length which can hang over the table without slipping is? (The vertical portion of table is smooth)",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{\\mu}{1 + \\mu}L$",
    "B": "$\\frac{1 - \\mu}{\\mu}L$",
    "C": "$\\frac{1 - \\mu}{1 + \\mu}L$",
    "D": "$\\mu L$"
  },
  "answer": {
